    "raw": "Given:\n- Total pages in the book: 500\n- Pages written in the first week: 150\n- Pages written in the second week: 30% of the remaining pages\n- Pages damaged by coffee spill: 20% of the empty pages\n\nStep 1: Calculate the remaining pages after the first week.\nRemaining pages after the first week = Total pages - Pages written in the first week\n= 500 - 150 = 350 pages\n\nStep 2: Calculate the pages written in the second week.\nPages written in the second week = 30% of remaining pages\n= 0.30 * 350 = 105 pages\n\nStep 3: Calculate the remaining pages after the second week.\nRemaining pages after the second week = Remaining pages after the first week - Pages written in the second week\n= 350 - 105 = 245 pages\n\nStep 4: Calculate the pages damaged by coffee spill.\nPages damaged by coffee spill = 20% of remaining pages\n= 0.20 * 245 = 49 pages\n\nStep 5: Calculate the total number of empty pages available for writing now.\nTotal empty pages available = Remaining pages after the second week - Pages damaged by coffee spill\n= 245 - 49 = 196 pages\n\nFINAL: 196",
